# 8. CARD SYSTEM

The card system is a major part of the gameplay.

It must support FOUR card categories.

## 8.1 Unit Cards

Deploy battlefield units.

Initial unit cards:

- Heavy Defender
- Swift Cavalry
- Arcane Archer
- Field Cleric

The system must also support future special units and summoned units.

## 8.2 Skill Cards

Immediately activate a combat effect.

Examples:

- Area damage
- Group healing
- Shield
- Crowd control
- Elemental damage

Skill effects must use the actual combat and status-effect systems.

## 8.3 Tactic Cards

Change friendly army behavior.

Examples:

- Full assault
- Focus fire
- Emergency defense
- Formation reinforcement
- Temporary attack boost

Tactic effects can be temporary or execute a single tactical command.

## 8.4 Support Cards

Provide temporary or persistent support effects.

Examples:

- Attack enhancement
- Defense enhancement
- Healing enhancement
- Energy recovery
- Temporary shield

Support effects must have clear targets and durations.

## 8.5 Deck and hand

Use a 12-card battle deck.

Display six cards in the existing tactical card area.

When a card is used:

- Remove it from the hand.
- Apply its effect.
- Draw the next card from the remaining deck.
- Respect energy, cooldown, and unit limits.

When the deck is exhausted, no additional cards can be drawn.

Existing hand and deck behavior must be inspected and integrated rather than replaced unnecessarily.

## 8.6 Card merging

Keep six card slots.

Two cards can merge only if:

- They have the same card ID.
- They have the same card level.
- They occupy adjacent slots.
- They are both eligible for merging.

Merge results:

- Two Level I cards → one Level II card.
- Two Level II cards → one Level III card.
- Level III is the current maximum.

Different cards cannot merge.

Different card categories cannot merge.

Do not merge cards with different identities just because they share a category.

Each card type must define its upgrade effect.

Examples:

- Unit card: deploy a stronger unit.
- Skill card: improve power or area.
- Tactic card: improve effect or duration.
- Support card: improve buff strength or target coverage.

Merging must not directly spawn a battlefield unit.

The player must be able to understand the merge result through clear UI feedback.

## 8.7 Card deployment

Unit cards spawn units in the friendly deployment region.

Support and tactic cards apply their configured effects.

Skill cards resolve their configured effects.

If deployment is invalid because of unit cap, insufficient energy, or cooldown:

- Do not consume the card.
- Do not consume energy.
- Show a clear explanation.

Prevent spawning outside the battlefield.

